# Cloudflare Workers static assets reads this file. Up to 100 rules, 2,000
# characters per line. It applies to assets, which is all this project serves:
# there is no "main" in wrangler.jsonc, so no Worker code ever runs.
#
# Deliberately one rule block. Two blocks matching the same path leaves the
# merge order deciding which header wins, and nothing here is worth that.
#
# No Cache-Control on purpose. The default for static assets is
# "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate" with an ETag, which is the right answer
# for a small site edited by hand: revalidation is cheap and an edit is never
# stuck behind a stale cache. Filenames are not content-hashed, so a long
# max-age here would serve old CSS after a deploy.
#
# The CSP is this strict because the site genuinely has nothing in it: no
# scripts, no web fonts, no frames, no forms, no third-party requests at all.
# If any of those are ever added, this line has to change with them.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

